cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use akróasys in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "akróasys"
abstract: >-
  akróasys is a synthesizer that uses generative AI as an oscillator rather than
  as a generator of finished audio. It carries two such oscillators. The T5
  Oscillator operates inside the text-embedding space of a diffusion audio model,
  before that space has been rendered to sound, and makes the embedding itself
  playable. The Language-Resonant Oscillator (LRO) takes a description in ordinary
  language and has a locally running language model write a complete Csound
  orchestra for it, against a curated library of parametrised synthesis code; the
  resulting program is compiled and executed live as the instrument's voice source.
  akróasys is developed as a critical-aesthetic and pedagogical instrument for
  making machine listening audible and playable.
authors:
